---
/**
 * GlossaryChrome.astro
 *
 * Site-local CSS for adtechglossary, imported and rendered by all four page
 * templates (index, [section]/index, [section]/[slug], 404). Every selector
 * is prefixed `:root[data-site='adtechglossary']` (specificity 0,2,N) so it
 * beats `packages/shared-ui/src/styles/global.css`'s element selectors
 * regardless of bundle order, without editing that frozen file.
 *
 * This component renders no markup of its own — its whole body is one
 * `<style is:global>` block.
 *
 * =====================================================================
 * THE NAMED EDITORIAL MOVE — "the sheet on the desk"
 * =====================================================================
 * The #f4f4f4 ground is a desk and every page is a single continuous
 * #ffffff SHEET laid on it: one page width (1180px) shared by the index
 * and by every entry, zero border, zero shadow, zero radius. The site's
 * one value jump (1.10:1, computed) is spent at PAGE scale instead of
 * being scattered across six small white rectangles — which is what it
 * used to be, and which is why the inversion, the site's stated dominant
 * differentiator, was barely legible.
 *
 * Three rules follow from it, and they are the whole design:
 *
 *   1. NOTHING INSIDE THE SHEET IS BOXED. The AnswerBox loses its ground,
 *      the blockquote loses its rule, the provenance note loses its dashed
 *      border, the section kicker loses its 24px pill. Hierarchy is scale,
 *      space and hairline only (editorial-references §1: "boxless
 *      hierarchy", Pudding live — 0 containers across 3 essays).
 *
 *   2. EVERY STRUCTURAL RULE SPANS THE FULL SHEET, and only headings that
 *      are direct children of the sheet get one. That is Monocle's live
 *      `1px solid var(--border-*)` between sections (30+ occurrences) and
 *      Raconteur's `.block-title { border-bottom: 1px solid #dee2e6 }`,
 *      used here as the page's architecture: the rules, not a container,
 *      draw the page edges.
 *
 *   3. THE MEASURE IS 72ch AND THE EVIDENCE USES THE REST. Running prose
 *      sits left at 72ch; tables, code panels and figures — 36 of 36 term
 *      pages carry a table — take the full 1068px sheet column and break
 *      into the right margin the prose leaves empty. The full-sheet rules
 *      are what make that margin read as a margin rather than as a gap.
 *
 * Type-role split (editorial-references §2.7, the NYT grotesque-for-
 * metadata mechanic): IBM Plex Sans carries the reading path — prose,
 * headings, term names — and IBM Plex Mono carries EVERYTHING that is not
 * the reading path: kicker, hatnote/breadcrumb, letter heads, table
 * captions, cell notes, provenance, answer source. Family alone separates
 * definition from sourcing, with no box and no icon.
 *
 * Accent budget: amber #845720 marks WAYFINDING and nothing else — the
 * brand square, the section kicker, the A-Z letter heads, the code
 * accent. It never appears on a rule, a ground or a button.
 *
 * NO DARK MODE. There is no OS-colour-scheme media block in this file or
 * anywhere under sites/adtechglossary/.
 */
---

<style is:global>
  /* ============================================================
   * 1 — THE SHEET
   *
   * `--sheet-pad` and the 1180px page width come from the token file.
   * `main.prose`'s cap is `--measure-max` (= the page width), NOT the
   * measure: the running-text cap is applied per element in §2 below, so
   * that tables and code can use the whole sheet. This replaces the old
   * negative-margin "breakout" of tables past a 72ch main — that trick
   * needed `100vw` arithmetic, a scrollbar correction and `overflow-x:
   * hidden` on the document root to stay on screen; all three are now
   * deleted, because nothing escapes the sheet any more.
   * ============================================================ */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > article,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .sheet {
    background: var(--cds-layer-01); /* #ffffff on the #f4f4f4 desk — 1.10:1, the device */
    padding: var(--sheet-pad);
    /* Deliberately absent, all three: border, box-shadow, border-radius.
       The value jump is the edge (spec §7.3 axis 4 — "background layering
       with zero shadow AND zero border"). */
  }

  /* The masthead is the one block that stays on the desk: it is the label
     on the folder, not a page in it. */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .masthead {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-07); /* 32px of desk before the sheet begins */
  }

  /* ============================================================
   * 2 — MEASURE: prose at 72ch, evidence at full sheet width
   * ============================================================ */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > article > p,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > article > ul,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > article > ol,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > article > dl,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > article > h3,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > article > h4,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > article > blockquote,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > article > .answer-box,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > article > .faq dl,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > article > .related ul,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .sheet > p,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .sheet > ul,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .sheet > ol,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .sheet > .faq dl,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .masthead > p,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .masthead > .answer-box {
    max-width: var(--site-measure); /* 72ch — the portfolio's widest, unchanged */
  }

  /* `.engagement p` reads `--measure-max` in global.css, which on this site
     is now the PAGE width, not the text measure. Re-point it at the real
     measure so the closing block wraps like the prose above it. */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .engagement p {
    max-width: var(--site-measure);
  }

  /* Tables, code panels and figures deliberately carry NO max-width: they
     fill the sheet column and run past the prose measure into the margin it
     leaves. This is the one place the page is asymmetric, and it is where
     the argument of every term page lives. */

  /* ============================================================
   * 3 — RULES: full-sheet hairlines, and only on top-level headings
   *
   * The bleed pair (negative inline margin + equal inline padding) makes an
   * element's own rule span the sheet while its text stays in the column.
   * The set is closed on purpose — a nested h2 (the FAQ heading, a contents
   * entry) gets no rule, so "a rule means a page-level break" stays true.
   * ============================================================ */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > article > h1,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > article > h2,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > article > .faq,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > article > .related,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > article > .engagement,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .sheet > h1,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .sheet > h2,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .sheet > .az-rail,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .sheet > .faq,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .sheet > .related,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .contents > section {
    margin-inline: calc(-1 * var(--sheet-pad));
    padding-inline: var(--sheet-pad);
  }

  /* The encyclopedia tell, kept and amplified: h1 and h2 are NOT bold, just
     larger, sitting on a neutral hairline (Wikipedia live, design-research
     §3.5). `--heading-rule` (#a8a8a8 — 2.38:1 on the sheet, 2.16:1 on the
     desk, both computed) is one step stronger than the structural
     `--border` because this rule is the loudest device on the site. */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > article > h1,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > article > h2,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .sheet > h1,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .sheet > h2,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .masthead > h1,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > h1 {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--heading-rule);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-03); /* 8px */
  }

  /* ============================================================
   * 4 — RHYTHM: asymmetric, rule-anchored (editorial-references §2.9 —
   * Stripe Press's live `margin: 80px 0 10px` immediately before a rule).
   * Big space ABOVE the break, small below: 48/16 at h2 (3:1), 40/8 at h3
   * (5:1). On a deliberately flat ≈1.8x type ramp, spacing IS the
   * hierarchy, so this is where the pass spends its budget — not on size.
   * ============================================================ */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > article > h1,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .sheet > h1,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .masthead > h1,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main > h1 {
    margin-block: 0 var(--space-06); /* 0 / 24px — the sheet's own padding is the space above */
  }

  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] h2 {
    margin-block: var(--space-layout-04) var(--space-05); /* 48 / 16 */
    padding-top: 0; /* kills global.css's 0.5rem heading padding-top */
  }

  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] h3 {
    margin-block: var(--space-08) var(--space-03); /* 40 / 8 */
  }

  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] h4 {
    margin-block: var(--space-06) var(--space-03); /* 24 / 8 */
  }

  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] p,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] ul,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] ol,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] dl {
    margin-block: 0 var(--space-05); /* 16px — was 1.1rem = 17.6px, off the 8px grid */
  }

  /* MUST-FIX (retained from the previous pass): this site's desktop ramp is
     ALREADY Carbon's stock ramp shifted one role down (h1 = Heading 02/32px,
     h2 = Heading 03/24px). global.css's portfolio-wide mobile rule shifts
     h1/h2 down ANOTHER role at <=640px, which double-demotes this site only:
     h1 lands at 24px (this site's own h2 size) and h2 at 20px/400, colliding
     in SIZE with h3's 20px/600 — a 1.41x ramp with a mid-scale collision, on
     the one site whose identity is a flat ~1.8x size-only ramp. Re-asserting
     the desktop sizes holds 32/24/20/18 across the breakpoint. */
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] h1 {
      font-size: var(--type-heading-01-size);
    }

    :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] h2 {
      font-size: var(--type-heading-02-size);
    }
  }

  /* ============================================================
   * 5 — THE HEADWORD UNIT: kicker, headword, lead
   *
   * A dictionary entry opens kicker / headword / rule / sense. All three
   * type roles are already in the chassis; what changes here is that none
   * of them is in a box any more.
   * ============================================================ */

  /* The kicker was a 24px amber pill. It is now Raconteur's live category
     kicker: tracked uppercase mono, no box, no background, sitting tight
     above the headword. This also retires the site's last rounded corner —
     see the --chip-radius note in the token file. */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .eyebrow {
    display: block;
    background: none;
    border-radius: 0;
    padding: 0;
    min-height: 0;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-02); /* 4px — the kicker belongs to the headword */
    color: var(--site-accent); /* #845720 on #ffffff — 6.24:1, computed */
  }

  /* The lead. `.answer-box` keeps its structural precedence (it still
     renders before body prose — AnswerBox.astro's GEO docblock, spec §12.5)
     and loses its ground: it already sat on #ffffff, so its own #ffffff
     rectangle was a box with no value jump behind it. Precedence is now
     scale + position + air: Heading 05 (20px/400, ibm.md:97) directly under
     the headword rule, then 32px of nothing. Wikipedia's unboxed lead. */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .answer-box {
    background: none;
    box-shadow: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-07); /* 32px */
  }

  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .answer-text {
    font-size: var(--type-heading-05-size); /* 20px */
    font-weight: var(--type-heading-05-weight); /* 400 */
    line-height: var(--type-heading-05-lh); /* 1.4 */
  }

  /* ============================================================
   * 6 — THE METADATA FACE (editorial-references §2.7)
   *
   * Plex Mono is promoted from "the label primitive" to this site's whole
   * non-prose voice. Every role below is sourcing, provenance or wayfinding
   * — never the definition itself, which stays Sans.
   * ============================================================ */

  /* Hatnote register (design-research §3.5, Wikipedia live: 13px, muted,
     UNBORDERED, above the lead). The breadcrumb IS this site's hatnote slot,
     and it sits on the desk, above the sheet — #525252 on #f4f4f4 = 7.10:1. */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .breadcrumbs ol {
    font-family: var(--meta-font);
    font-size: var(--hatnote-size);
    color: var(--hatnote-color);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-05);
  }

  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .breadcrumbs li + li::before {
    color: var(--cds-text-placeholder); /* #6f6f6f on #f4f4f4 — 4.57:1 */
  }

  /* Terse caption directly under (here: over) the figure, method deferred —
     editorial-references §2.13, Pudding live. */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] caption {
    font-family: var(--meta-font);
    font-size: var(--meta-size);
    letter-spacing: 0;
    color: var(--cds-text-secondary); /* #525252 on #ffffff — 7.81:1 */
    padding-bottom: var(--space-03);
  }

  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .cell-note {
    font-family: var(--meta-font);
    font-size: var(--meta-size);
  }

  /* Provenance. Was a dashed 1px box — the one dashed border on the site,
     and a box on a boxless page. It becomes a mono credit line under a
     hairline, which is the figure-in-a-paper convention this corpus
     actually wants. */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .spec-source {
    border: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: none;
    border-radius: 0;
    padding: var(--space-04) 0 0; /* 12px */
    margin: var(--space-07) 0 var(--space-06);
    font-family: var(--meta-font);
    font-size: var(--meta-size);
    color: var(--cds-text-secondary);
  }

  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .answer-source {
    font-family: var(--meta-font);
    font-size: var(--meta-size);
  }

  /* One label primitive, not two: global.css's `.footer-block h2` ships a
     SANS uppercase 0.08em treatment that competes with the mono wayfinding
     label used everywhere else on this site. */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .footer-block h2 {
    font-family: var(--meta-font);
    font-size: var(--label-size);
    letter-spacing: var(--track-label);
    font-weight: var(--label-weight);
    border-bottom: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* ============================================================
   * 7 — TABLES: the interior main event (36/36 term pages)
   * ============================================================ */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main table {
    background: transparent; /* the sheet is already the ground */
    margin-block: var(--space-06) var(--space-07);
  }

  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main th,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main td {
    border: 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); /* horizontal rules only — no vertical grid */
    padding: var(--space-03) var(--space-04); /* 8 / 12 */
    font-size: var(--type-body-long-01-size); /* 16px/1.5, Carbon Body Long 01 */
    line-height: var(--lh-ui);
  }

  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main thead th {
    background: var(--cds-layer-02); /* #e0e0e0 — the INSET band, the ramp read downward */
    font-size: var(--type-body-short-02-size); /* 14px/600/+0.16px, spec §9.5 verbatim */
    font-weight: var(--type-body-short-02-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--type-body-short-02-tracking);
    text-transform: none; /* uppercase belongs to the mono label primitive only */
  }

  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main tbody th[scope='row'] {
    background: transparent;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* MEASURED FIX (retained): #3366cc on the thead's #e0e0e0 inset band is
     4.07:1, under the 4.5:1 floor. Interactive text moves to the sheet,
     where the same ink is 5.37:1. Interactive = raised, inert = inset. */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main thead th a {
    background: var(--cds-layer-01);
  }

  /* Inline code: THE DESK SHOWING THROUGH THE SHEET.
     `global.css` fills inline `code` with `--bg-inset` (#e0e0e0 here), which
     on a page whose Fields column carries six literals per row reads as
     confetti — a run of little grey boxes on a page whose whole premise is
     that nothing is boxed. Moving the fill one step up to the DESK colour
     (#f4f4f4, exactly the ground the sheet is lying on) keeps the literal
     marked without a box reading, and reuses a mechanic the site already
     has: the table row hover and the code panel are the same idea at
     different depths.
     It also RETIRES a WCAG workaround instead of papering over one. The
     documented failing pair was a link inside inline code — #3366cc on
     #e0e0e0 = 4.07:1 — which used to be fixed by lifting that code onto
     #ffffff. On #f4f4f4 the same link measures 4.88:1 and the visited state
     4.88:1, both PASS, so the lift rule is deleted rather than kept as dead
     weight. (The `thead th a` lift above stays: a bare link in a header cell
     sits on the band itself, not on a code chip.) */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] code {
    background: var(--cds-background); /* #f4f4f4 — link 4.88:1, visited 4.88:1, ink 16.45:1 */
    padding: 0.1em 0.3em;
  }

  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] pre code {
    background: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  /* At <=640px `global.css` turns the table into its own scroll container
     (`display:block; width:auto; max-width:100%; overflow-x:auto`, preserved
     verbatim per spec §12.7). That containment was being defeated inside the
     cells: `:not(pre) > code { overflow-wrap: anywhere }` let schema
     identifiers break mid-token, so `package_id` rendered as "pack / age_i /
     d" down a 60px column instead of making the table scroll. Holding code
     tokens intact hands the overflow back to the scroll container that was
     built for it. Scoped to the width where that container exists. */
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main table :not(pre) > code,
    :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main table code {
      overflow-wrap: normal;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
  }

  @media (hover: hover) {
    :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main tbody tr:hover {
      background: var(--cds-background); /* the desk shows through the sheet */
    }
  }

  /* ============================================================
   * 8 — LINKS: underline discipline + the same measured WCAG fix
   * ============================================================ */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main a {
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  }

  /* Blocks that are ENTIRELY links carry no ambiguity about which words are
     links, so the underline comes off at rest and back on hover/focus —
     Wikipedia's own index/nav behaviour, applied by rule, not blanket
     removal. */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .az-run a,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .term-list a,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .related a,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .portfolio-links a,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .breadcrumbs a,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .contents h2 a,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .az-rail a {
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .az-run a:hover,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .az-run a:focus-visible,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .term-list a:hover,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .term-list a:focus-visible,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .related a:hover,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .related a:focus-visible,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .contents h2 a:hover,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .contents h2 a:focus-visible,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .breadcrumbs a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  }

  /* The `a code, a > code { background: #ffffff }` lift that used to live
     here is DELETED, not moved: inline code now sits on #f4f4f4 (see §7),
     where a link measures 4.88:1 and a visited link 4.88:1 — both PASS
     without lifting anything. Recorded so nobody re-adds it. */

  /* Do not suppress :visited anywhere — in the A-Z run it is the site's most
     valuable affordance at 35 terms, and it is the portfolio's only visited
     state. (No rule here; this comment documents the deliberate absence.) */

  /* ============================================================
   * 9 — QUOTATION AND THE CLOSING BLOCKS: no boxes, no left rules
   * ============================================================ */

  /* Block quotations are frequent in this corpus (specification text quoted
     verbatim). They were a bordered, tinted panel; they are now an indented
     quotation in the secondary ink, which is what a reference work does with
     quoted source text. No rule of any weight — the site's rules are
     horizontal and architectural, and a vertical one would read as a second,
     competing system (and slop tell 4). */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] blockquote {
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    color: var(--cds-text-secondary); /* #525252 on #ffffff — 7.81:1 */
    margin: var(--space-06) 0;
    padding: 0 0 0 var(--space-07); /* 32px hanging indent */
    max-width: var(--site-measure);
  }

  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .faq,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .related {
    margin-top: var(--space-layout-05); /* 64px — the region break, above its rule */
    padding-top: var(--space-06);
  }

  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .engagement {
    border-left: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    margin-block: var(--space-layout-05) 0; /* 64px */
    padding-block: var(--space-06) var(--space-02);
  }

  /* ============================================================
   * 10 — SQUARING THE SHARED COMPONENTS
   * Three shared rules hardcode a radius the 0px law does not permit.
   * They are corrected by cascade here, never by editing shared-ui.
   * ============================================================ */

  /* global.css's `.brand-mark` is a 14px rounded square (3px). On the only
     0px-radius site the masthead mark is a SQUARE of amber — which is also
     the only place the accent appears in the chrome. */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .brand-mark {
    border-radius: 0;
  }

  /* global.css's `.badge` hardcodes `--radius-2`. */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .badge {
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  /* Footer.astro hardcodes `border-radius: var(--radius-2, 2px)` on the
     focus ring of `.brand-mark-link` and `.portfolio-links a`. */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .brand-mark-link,
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] .portfolio-links a:focus-visible {
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  /* Most links in this site's own markup inherit no explicit focus treatment
     and fall through to the UA default outline, which on Chromium is
     literally system blue — the one hue this portfolio deletes everywhere
     else (ruling 4). One rule covers all of them since they share the <main>
     ancestor. */
  :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] main a:focus-visible {
    outline: none;
    box-shadow: var(--focus-ring);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  /* ============================================================
   * 11 — MOTION
   * ============================================================ */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    :root[data-site='adtechglossary'] {
      scroll-behavior: auto;
    }
  }

  /* ============================================================
   * 12 — THE LETTER RAIL + A-Z INDEX (homepage)
   *
   * (a) `auto-fit` with a 26-cell alphabet always wraps to >=2 UNEVEN rows,
   *     orphaning a lone "Z". Forcing exactly 13 columns once the rail is
   *     sticky makes it a DELIBERATE two-row block (A-M / N-Z). 13 columns
   *     clear 44px at any sticky width.
